<main class="eg-page"><div class="eg-wrap"><nav class="eg-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Agency brief & RFP template</span></nav><section class="eg-hero" aria-labelledby="eg-title"><div><p class="eg-kicker">Free B2B lead generation RFP template</p><h1 id="eg-title">Give every lead generation agency the same clear brief.</h1><p class="eg-lead">Define the buyers, work and meeting requirements before you ask for quotes. Build a brief you can copy, print and send to the agencies you want to consider.</p><div class="eg-actions"><a class="eg-button" href="#brief-builder">Build My Agency Brief ↓</a><a class="eg-link" href="/assets/downloads/CallTeam-Lead-Generation-RFP-Template.txt" download>Download the blank template ↓</a></div><p class="eg-small">Free. No account or email required. Editable plain-text downloads.</p></div><aside class="eg-cover" aria-label="What the agency brief establishes"><p class="eg-kicker">Before the proposals arrive</p><h2>Make the request specific.</h2><dl><div><dt>The audience</dt><dd>Who fits, where they operate and which buyer matters.</dd></div><div><dt>The responsibility</dt><dd>What the agency handles and what your team retains.</dd></div><div><dt>The response</dt><dd>Qualification, reporting, costs and open requirements.</dd></div></dl><p class="eg-cover-note">Create the brief here. Compare the proposals when they arrive.</p></aside></section></div>
<div class="eg-answer"><div class="eg-wrap"><p><strong>A lead generation RFP is a request for proposal:</strong> a brief that lets agencies respond to the same campaign requirements. Use this resource for B2B appointment setting, cold calling or outsourced SDR work, with a formal procurement process or a straightforward buying conversation.</p></div></div>
<nav class="eg-wrap eg-jump" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#brief-builder">Create the brief</a><a href="#brief-example">Completed example</a><a href="#brief-response">Agency questions</a><a href="#brief-compare">After the quotes</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></nav>
<section class="eg-section eg-paper" id="brief-builder"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">Six short fields</p><h2>Start with the campaign you want to buy.</h2><p>The first five fields are required. Timing and budget can stay open. Keep confidential client names and sensitive records out of the brief.</p></div><noscript><p class="eg-error">Enable JavaScript to assemble a personalised brief. The blank template, fictional example and agency response checklist remain available without it.</p></noscript>
<div id="eg-brief-form" class="eg-input-area" role="group" aria-label="Your agency brief requirements" data-clarity-mask="true"><div class="eg-fields">
<label class="eg-field" for="brief-offer"><span>1. What do you sell?</span><input id="brief-offer" type="text" maxlength="240" required placeholder="For example: ERP software for distributors"><small>State the product or service and the customer problem. Up to 240 characters.</small></label>
<label class="eg-field" for="brief-buyer"><span>2. Who do you want to reach?</span><input id="brief-buyer" type="text" maxlength="140" required placeholder="For example: CFOs at wholesale distributors"><small>A job role and the type of company. Up to 140 characters.</small></label>
<label class="eg-field" for="brief-market"><span>3. Which market?</span><input id="brief-market" type="text" maxlength="140" required placeholder="For example: US and Canadian distributors"><small>Include relevant territory or language requirements. Up to 140 characters.</small></label>
<label class="eg-field" for="brief-work"><span>4. What work should the agency cover?</span><select id="brief-work" required><option value="">Choose the work</option><option>Research and calling</option><option>Calling an existing list</option><option>Research, calling and follow-up</option></select><small>Use this starting description, then confirm the detailed responsibilities.</small></label>
<label class="eg-field" for="brief-criteria"><span>5. What would make a meeting useful?</span><textarea id="brief-criteria" maxlength="400" required rows="4" placeholder="For example: A relevant finance owner, a reporting issue to explore and agreement to a discovery call"></textarea><small>Describe fit, buyer involvement and the purpose. Up to 400 characters.</small></label>
<label class="eg-field" for="brief-timing"><span>6. Timing and budget, if known</span><textarea id="brief-timing" maxlength="200" rows="4" placeholder="Optional: desired start, budget range or proposal deadline"></textarea><small>Leave blank if you want agencies to state their proposed terms. Up to 200 characters.</small></label>
</div><div class="eg-actions"><button type="button" class="eg-button" id="eg-brief-run" disabled>Create My Brief →</button><button type="button" class="eg-button eg-secondary" id="eg-brief-example" disabled>Load an Example</button><button type="button" class="eg-button eg-secondary" id="eg-brief-reset" disabled>Clear Fields</button></div><p class="eg-small">The builder runs in your browser. Inputs and output are masked from session replay. Copy or print to keep your brief; it is not sent with a booking.</p><p id="eg-brief-status" role="status" class="eg-status"></p></div>
<section id="eg-brief-results" class="eg-result" aria-labelledby="eg-brief-title" data-clarity-mask="true" hidden><p class="eg-kicker">Your campaign requirements</p><h2 id="eg-brief-title" tabindex="-1">Your agency brief is ready to review.</h2><p>Check the wording, add any exclusions and confirm the open requirements before sharing it. No agency has received this brief.</p><div class="eg-actions"><button type="button" class="eg-button eg-secondary" id="eg-brief-copy">Copy My Brief</button><button type="button" class="eg-button eg-secondary" id="eg-brief-print">Print My Brief</button></div><p id="eg-brief-copy-status" class="eg-status" role="status"></p><label class="eg-field" for="eg-brief-output"><span>Your brief text to select and copy</span></label><textarea id="eg-brief-output" rows="24" readonly spellcheck="false"></textarea><pre id="eg-brief-print-copy" class="eg-print-copy"></pre><p class="eg-small">This buying brief is a starting document. Agree commercial terms and obligations separately.</p><a class="eg-link" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discuss My Campaign Brief ↗</a></section>
<div class="eg-download"><div><strong>Prefer to work in your own document editor?</strong><p>Download the editable template or use the completed fictional example as a guide.</p></div><div class="eg-actions"><a class="eg-link" href="/assets/downloads/CallTeam-Lead-Generation-RFP-Template.txt" download>Blank template ↓</a><a class="eg-link" href="/assets/downloads/CallTeam-Agency-Brief-Example.txt" download>Completed example ↓</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="eg-section" id="brief-example"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">A fictional ERP provider</p><h2>A request agencies can actually respond to.</h2><p>This example shows the level of detail needed for an initial response. It represents no real client or agency proposal.</p></div><div class="eg-grid"><article class="eg-card"><h3>The campaign request</h3><p>ERP software for wholesale distributors in the US and Canada. Reach CFOs and finance leaders. Include research, human calling and follow-up.</p><p><strong>A useful meeting:</strong> a suitable distributor, a relevant finance owner, a confirmed reporting question and agreement to an introductory conversation.</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>The information still needed</h3><p>Ask each agency for account exclusions, data preparation, caller responsibilities, meeting notes, fees, launch dependencies and the client's role.</p><p>An itemised response makes those choices visible before anyone commits to the campaign.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="eg-section eg-paper" id="brief-response"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">Put these questions beside the brief</p><h2>Ask for a response with useful detail.</h2></div><div class="eg-grid eg-three"><article class="eg-card"><h3>Account selection</h3><p>Which companies belong in the campaign, what is excluded and how will contact records be prepared?</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Execution ownership</h3><p>Who researches, calls, handles agreed follow-up, qualifies and schedules? What must your team provide?</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Meeting definition</h3><p>What confirms the buyer's agreement? How are no-shows, unsuitable meetings and rejection reasons handled?</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Reporting and handoff</h3><p>Which notes and records reach sales, how often are results reviewed and what access is agreed?</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Commercial terms</h3><p>What is the fixed fee, billing period, preparation cost, variable charge and minimum commitment?</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Relevant evidence</h3><p>Which past campaign resembles your audience and sales motion? What period and definitions support its reported result?</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="eg-section" id="brief-compare"><div class="eg-wrap eg-split"><div><p class="eg-kicker">When the responses arrive</p><h2>Compare the proposals against the same request.</h2><p>Use one currency and comparison period, then examine costs, meeting definitions and work included. Keep unanswered terms visible so the next conversation can resolve them.</p><a class="eg-button" href="/lead-generation-proposal-comparison/">Compare Your Agency Proposals →</a></div><div class="eg-card"><h3>Make the wider buying decision.</h3><p>The service buying guide explains delivery models and provider selection. The ROI Calculator helps you test campaign economics using your own inputs.</p><p><a class="eg-link" href="/articles/b2b-lead-generation-services/">Read the agency buying guide →</a></p><a class="eg-link" href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/">Calculate Your Campaign ROI →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="eg-section eg-paper"><div class="eg-wrap eg-split"><div><p class="eg-kicker">A scoped response from CallTeam</p><h2>Bring the brief. Let’s discuss the work.</h2><p>CallTeam can assess prospect research, human calling, follow-up, qualification, appointment setting and sales handoff around your requirements. We will identify what needs confirming before the campaign is ready to run.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/services/">Explore CallTeam services →</a></div><div><h3>See evidence before choosing.</h3><p>Read the audience, execution and reported outcomes in our <a href="/case-studies/">campaign case studies</a>. Check <a href="/pricing/">current pricing</a> alongside a written scope.</p><p>When a campaign is agreed, the <a href="/b2b-cold-calling-starter-kit/">Cold Calling Starter Kit</a> gives your team working documents for preparation and call tracking.</p></div></div></section>
